WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.534
-Oh, I'm so happy you're here.
Welcome.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.968
-Oh, my God, I'm so happy
to be here,

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:06.400
and your opening was everything.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.234
-Oh, my gosh. I can't even talk
to you right now.

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:11.334
-I was, like, crying in the back
just laughing so hard.

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:12.968
It was fantastic.

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:15.300
-I got to say, wearing that
sweatshirt felt pretty good.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.667
I mean, you rocked it, clearly.

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:19.033
This right here was --

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:21.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:24.367
This was actually based on
your actual sweatshirt, right?

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:28.067
-Yeah, it was an accident. It
was based on a fashion accident.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:31.000
I had my favorite sweatshirt
in high school.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.434
And I put it in the dryer for
too long and at really high heat

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:36.667
so the neck part shrunk and I
couldn't get my head through it.

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:40.601
So I just cut out the hole
and I wore it

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:43.734
to a wardrobe fitting
for "Flashdance."

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.133
And Adrian Lyne, the director,
really loved it.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.400
And Michael Kaplan, the costume
designer, loved it.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.133
So he just made a much better
version of it for the film.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.934
-And then it became
totally iconic.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:54.968
You're like, "Yeah, that's me."

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.267
Do you have this sweatshirt
still?

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.601
-Yeah, it's in storage
somewhere.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:58.767
-Good. I love that, yeah.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.634
-And also that red band jacket
thing.

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.567
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, I have that somewhere.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:06.167
-I read a story once about --
tell me if it's true.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:09.267
When you auditioned for
"Flashdance," you got it,

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:12.234
but you were like, "I'm also --
I really want to go to school."

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:15.234
-Yes, yeah, yeah.
-And school, I will say Yale.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.167
-Yes, yeah.
-So, that's a real school.

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:19.734
Wow, so, you were like,
"I don't know what to do."

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:24.000
-Well, yeah. I mean, the
audition process was very long,

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.868
and I kind of -- I have to say
I did enjoy it

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:29.000
because I never thought it would
happen, you know?

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.901
And once I got to school, my
agent called the dean, I think,

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:38.000
because I didn't have a phone
and got me the message saying

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.634
you know that
"you got the part."

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:42.834
And I was, like, "Okay.

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.667
I have to think about this
for a moment.

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:47.300
Let me just take the weekend
to think about it."

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.801
-Yeah, because you didn't know
what's gonna happen with
"Flashdance."

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:51.033
-I could hear her silent scream
on the other end of the phone.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:53.601
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:56.334
-But then you did it,
and you go -- Did you know

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:58.901
it was going to be a big hit
or change your life or no?

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:00.601
You just kind of --
-I didn't even think that way.

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.868
I didn't think that way at all.
-You're just, "I'm just going to

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.400
do this and then --"
-Yeah, I'll do this thing,

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.801
and I'll go back to school.

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:07.567
-But then the soundtrack.
Then it was everything.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.133
It was part of everyone's life.
You're like,

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:11.300
"Oh, this is actually bigger
than I could even imagine."

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.934
-Yeah, it was like this weird
meta experience

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:15.767
when you're walking down the
street and you see everybody

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:18.934
in the cutoff sweatshirts.
It was an interesting moment.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:21.734
-Why do you think it was
so popular with everyone?

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:25.634
-I think because it was really
aspirational and it really

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:28.300
encouraged people to go
after their dreams.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.501
I mean, I got letters from,
like, lawyers who decided

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:34.701
to quit their jobs so they could
go and become this other thing

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.567
that they had always dreamt of.

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.667
-Follow your dreams
and work hard.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:41.167
-Yeah, yeah.
-It makes you feel good
when you watch it.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:43.033
Let's talk about your new movie,

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.267
"Luckiest Girl Alive"
on Netflix.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.167
And also I should mention
your series,

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:49.834
"The L-Word: Generation Q,"
which you star in

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.968
and executive produce.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.734
Returns for season three
on Showtime November 18th.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.200
Congrats on that.
-Thank you.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.567
-What can we say
about season three?

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.634
-As always, it's about love.

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.934
And there are some
true parenting challenges

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:05.167
that Bette and Tina have.

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.167
-I heard you say before
it's about love.

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:10.067
It's about getting love
or finding love

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.167
or what can we do for love.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.100
Love is the highest thing.
-Yeah. Yes.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.701
The "L" is also for love.

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:16.934
-Yeah. I do love.

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:19.400
Speaking of the letter "L,"
"Luckiest Girl Alive" premieres

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.834
Friday on Netflix, based on
the best-selling novel.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.767
Can you tell everybody
who you play?

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.701
-I play LoLo Vincent.

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:27.200
-Yeah. That's a great name.
-I do.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:29.667
-Yeah.
She's a fantastic character.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:33.801
The movie stars the goddess
known as Mila Kunis.

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:36.200
-Oh, we love Mila Kunis.
-We love Mila Kunis.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.300
And she's phenomenal.
-You two together too.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.634
-I played her mom once,
so this is really interesting.

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:43.834
Like, I've had like
a little trajectory.

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:46.033
-Isn't that hilarious?
-Yeah. I loved it.

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.067
Well, I love her.
She's a total girls girl,

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:50.634
and she's brilliant
and she's a great leader on set.

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:52.634
She also produced the film.

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:56.934
But she plays a character called
Ani Fanelli.

00:03:56.934 --> 00:04:01.734
And Ani is living this seemingly
Instagram-perfect life where she

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:05.100
has this sought-after job
at a glossy magazine.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.767
She's brilliant.
She's beautiful.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:09.734
She's engaged to this wealthy
guy who loves her.

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:12.234
And they're going to have this
fantasy wedding in Nantucket.

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:15.634
But you understand through
the voice-over in the film that

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:18.434
her internal dialogue
is at complete odds

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:20.501
with this seemingly perfect life
that she has.

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:22.234
So you know that there's
going to be this reckoning.

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:25.367
And then in walks this person
from her past

00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:29.634
who makes her confront
her secrets.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:32.534
-Yeah.
-And so it becomes a story about

00:04:32.534 --> 00:04:35.367
a woman who, in confronting
their past,

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:37.300
finds their voice
in the present.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.701
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:40.734
Here's Jennifer Beals
in "Luckiest Girl Alive."

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:42.067
Take a look at this.

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.934
-Miss Fanelli.

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:45.200
Right at home, I see.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.734
I need three to five cover line
tries for

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:49.434
the simultaneous-orgasm story by
the time I get back from lunch.

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:58.067
LoLo Vincent, editor and chief
of the "Women's Vibe."

00:04:58.067 --> 00:05:00.501
-Aaron Wickersham,
independent filmmaker.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:02.033
-Oh, that's right.

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:04.434
I saw your short at the Toronto
Film Festival a few years back.

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:07.200
Are you our hot guy of the month
for December?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.067
-Actually, I'm working on
a documentary

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:11.100
about gun violence in schools.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.067
I'm hoping to talk to...
-Don't say it.

00:05:14.067 --> 00:05:17.100
-...Tiffany.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.868
-I always forget
that's your name.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.934
-Well, Ani's pithier.

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:25.367
-Jennifer Beals, everybody!

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:29.067
"Luckiest Girl Alive" premieres
this Friday on Netflix.

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:32.300
And "The L-Word: Generation Q"
returns to Showtime

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.534
November 18th.

00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:35.968
Lea Thompson joins us
after the break.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.133
Stick around, everybody!

